# Tells GitHub Pages to serve this repository as-is instead of running Jekyll.
#
# Without it Jekyll silently drops every path whose name starts with "_", and
# two of those are load-bearing: js/domain/_value.js (imported by eight
# modules) and data/skills/shared/_node_schema.md (part of four prompts). A
# 404 anywhere in an ES module graph fails the WHOLE graph, so the deployed
# site rendered its static layout and ran no JavaScript at all.
#
# Nothing local can catch this: serve.py serves the underscore files happily,
# so every test passed while the public site was dead. scripts/check-deploy.mjs
# is the check that looks at what the host actually serves.
